# CLAUDE.md — {{PROJECT_NAME}} development conventions

Project conventions for work within this repository. Follow the host's instruction hierarchy and
the user's current scope, allowed actions, and approval conditions. This file does not override
those instructions or grant additional authority. Reuse applicable decisions and approvals from
the conversation; a helper skill does not reset them. Implementation authorization persists across
necessary source/plan/test edits within its approved scope; a changed working head requires refreshed
evidence where affected, not a new implementation approval.

Read-only investigations preserve audited resources and external systems. Necessary isolated disposable
fixtures, temporary reports and browser/test caches are allowed within the investigation unless the
user forbids those writes. Keep them separate from live/audited state. An explicit no-write-anywhere
instruction forbids even disposable fixture and cache writes.

Read/report/draft requests do not imply implementation or external publication. Before an action,
check its authorization, target, reviewed content, and applicable risk gate. AUTO is not permission;
REQUIRE needs matching human approval. Complete authorized reversible work without unnecessary
questions. A confirmed no-effect failure may be retried under unchanged authorization after checks;
an uncertain remote result needs read-only inspection first. Never repeat an already applied action.

---

## 0. How to read this — don't mix enforced (gate) with advisory (judgment)

| Marker | Meaning | Where it's enforced |
|---|---|---|
| ✅ **Gate** | A machine blocks the merge. Violation = RED | lint · typecheck · test · {{VERIFY_COMMAND}} |
| 🔶 **Guidance** | Needs judgment. Lives only as prose here | code review + agent judgment |

Lesson behind this split: a one-line fact from official docs becomes a gate; a design opinion becomes
guidance. Don't blur the two — "enforce a design opinion via lint" produces gates nobody can satisfy,
and "leave a hard factual constraint as prose" produces violations nobody catches.

